y include:\n- `jobTitles` (array of strings, exactly 1 item)\n- `locations` (array of UK strings, exactly 1 item)\n- `employmentType` (array)\n- `under10Applicants` (boolean)\n- `easyApply` (boolean)\n- `industryIds` (array)\n- `postedLimit` (string)\n- `sortBy` (string)\n- `maxItems` (number)\n\nDo not include `experienceLevel`.\nDo not include `workplaceType`.\nDo not invent additional fields.\n\nLOCATION RULES\n\n- Only UK locations\n- Extract the strongest city-level UK location from the profile when available\n- Use `\"United Kingdom\"` only if no useful UK city can be extracted or if a broader fallback is clearly justified\n- Ignore non-UK locations\n\nSTRATEGIC STRUCTURE\n\nGenerate exactly 2 configurations:\n\n1. Core Alignment Configuration\n- Highest-probability role framing\n- Strongest explicit profile alignment\n- `postedLimit = \"24h\"`\n\n2. Early Signal Configuration\n- Slightly broader but still defensible adjacent framing\n- `under10Applicants = true`\n- `postedLimit = \"1h\"`\n\nThe two configurations must use different job titles.\n\nDo not multiply breadth by adding extra titles or locations.\nUse role framing carefully within the fixed volume budget.\n\nOptimise for result quality within a hard cap, not raw surface area.\n\nBe deterministic.\nBe minimal.\nBe strict.\n"
